{
  "abstract": "We classify the rational points over $\\mathbb Q(r)$ on the genus-three cover $v^2=N_r(u)$, $a^2=(r^2-1)(1-u^2)$, where $N_r(u)=(r^4+2r+1)u^4+2r^2(r+1)u^3-r^2(2r+1)u^2-2r^4u+r^4$. This cover records a necessary paired norm and the anchor square in an explicitly defined determinant-zero Diophantine chart. Its only rational points are the four points with $u=\\pm1$ and $a=0$. We identify the elliptic norm quotient as a rational elliptic surface, prove that its geometric Mordell-Weil group has a saturated rank-two basis and trivial torsion, and classify every anchor-lifting lattice point. At infinity, a genus-two degeneration maps to a rank-zero elliptic curve and confines the lattice to five lines. At zero, an all-integer formal-group calculation reduces those lines to four degenerate points. Exact symbolic certificates and independent Sage and PARI audits support the proof. Consequently this chart has no nondegenerate septuple section with $r$ as rational base parameter. We also give a nonzero-anchor degree-two rational base change of the weaker cover and prove that it fails the next splitting condition by the constant squareclass three. The result does not exclude isolated rational fibres, further base changes, other charts, or rational Diophantine septuples.",
